-- title:
--   Frobenius lift and decomposition G_K=bigcup φⁿ I G_M
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $K$ be an intermediate field of the algebraic closure $\mathbb{Q}_p \subseteq$ `PadicAlgCl p` which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_p$. The assertion is the existence of a natural number $f$ and a $\mathbb{Q}_p$-algebra automorphism $\varphi$ of `PadicAlgCl p` such that: $f > 0$; $\varphi$ lies in the fixing subgroup of $K$, i.e. fixes $K$ pointwise; $\|\varphi x - x^{p^f}\| < 1$ for every $x$ in the closed unit ball $\|x\| \le 1$ of `PadicAlgCl p`, so that $\varphi$ lifts the $p^f$-power map on the residue field; and, for every intermediate field $M$ of $\mathbb{Q}_p \subseteq$ `PadicAlgCl p` that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_p$ and every $\mathbb{Q}_p$-automorphism $\sigma$ fixing $K$ pointwise, there are a natural number $n$ and automorphisms $\iota, \delta$ with $\sigma = \varphi^n \, \iota \, \delta$, where $\iota$ fixes $K$ pointwise and belongs to `(padicIntegers p).inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ_[p]`, the image in the full automorphism group of the inertia subgroup of the valuation subring of the canonical valuation on `PadicAlgCl p` (pushed forward along the inclusion of its decomposition subgroup), and $\delta$ fixes both $K$ and $M$ pointwise. Note that the exponent $n$ ranges over $\mathbb{N}$ only, not over $\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   This is the finite-level form of the statement that $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p/K)$ is generated by the inertia subgroup together with a Frobenius lift $\varphi$, the quotient by inertia being topologically generated by Frobenius; the cited characterisation of inertia as the automorphisms $\sigma$ with $\|\sigma x - x\| < 1$ on the unit ball is what makes the two displayed norm conditions comparable. It is used in the analysis of representations that are trivial on inertia, where a Frobenius-plus-inertia decomposition reduces statements about the whole local Galois group to statements about $\varphi$.
